{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/165057-the-triat-in-vtm","id":165057,"title":"The Triat in VTM","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-10T12:54:03-07:00","id":165057,"title":"The Triat in VTM","content":"I find it odd that Vampire is left without the Metaphysics Trinity/Triat that the other games hold closely. I woder how one would make a change to noddist lore to include the Triat. I have some vague Ideas, but nothing that would constitute a full addition (Blood being dynamasism, the Man being Stasis, and the Beast as Entropy). I just like the Idea that the World is the Same between the Cainites, Garou, and Mages; but Viewed through a different lens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3252-anutari","name":"Anutari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T13:13:47-07:00","id":165069,"title":"","content":"The only game that holds to the Triat is Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Mage has something similar with its dynamism, stasis, and entropy, but that's not quite the same thing.<br /> <br /> Vampire, Wraith, Changeilng, Hunter, Demon, and Orpheus don't include any concept of the Triat in their setting assumptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T20:40:41-07:00","id":166500,"title":"","content":"Vampire - Don't give a shit.<br /> Mage - Close second<br /> Wraith - Only the Wyrm. Called Gorool, it's a minion of Oblivion.<br /> Changeling - Not sure, I'm still reading through the 1st ed corebook.<br /> Hunter- The Messengers I think are more for God instead of the Trait or Gaia.<br /> Mummy - Another Wyrm only. This time called Apophis.<br /> Demon - More focused on Hell and the Earthbound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T07:56:50-07:00","id":166933,"title":"","content":"Gorool wouldn't be the Wyrm. If memory serves, Gorool is Charon's shadow. if anything in Wraith is the Wyrm, it's Oblivion itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1082-nfi","name":"NFI","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T09:37:31-07:00","id":166993,"title":"","content":"The Wyrm is a laughable imitation of the Oblivion in Wraith, For even a defiled spirit fears the nothingness that awaits slumbering beyond (and within) all dogma. Changelings have a mirror of the Wyld in Glamour and the Weaver in Banality (a better mirror exists in the DA:Fae, but that would take awhile to explain). Vampire has its own trinity of Caine, Lilith, and Lucifer if you want to look at it that way. Metaphysical natures notwithstanding, the universe is hardly an easy thing to deduce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1604-oliver-the-bold","name":"Oliver the Bold","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T11:26:56-07:00","id":167102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/165057-the-triat-in-vtm?p=166500#post166500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunter- The Messengers I think are more for God instead of the Trait or Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Things got weird, there, and the most prominent patrons of the Imbued were named as the Shadow Man and Burning Woman, aka the Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Queen from KotE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T11:36:04-07:00","id":167107,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I think the Entropy-Stasis-Dynamism (ESD) vs. Wyrm-Weaver-Wyld (WWW) parallel is interesting from an in-story perspective. Mages, regardless of paradigm, seem to understand that these forces represent abstract metaphysical laws of the Tellurian.<br /> <br /> Werewolves, on the other hand, are critters [sic] who come from a tribal and animistic society and have a natural affinity for Umbral travel. It\u2019s not hard to imagine that werecritters have observed these phenomena over eons and given them apocryphal, anthropomorphized characteristics. Entropy comes from the Wyrm, in this world-view, in much the same way as lightning comes from Zeus or nocturnal emissions come from succubi.<br /> <br /> As far as the other denizens of the WoD are concerned, they (as a sociocultural entity) probably haven\u2019t been able to observe ESD/WWW in any meaningful and conclusive way. At least not on the same scope the Werefolk have observed and Mages have studied. <br /> <br /> My two shekels on the subject.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T12:01:22-07:00","id":167124,"title":"","content":"While the Metaphysical Trinity (Dynamism, Stasis, and Entropy) is practically identical to the Wyld, Weaver, and Wyrm, the two are <i>not</i> the same. The Metaphysical Trinity is a classification of observed <i>forces</i> in the Tellurian, while the Wyld, Weaver, and Wyrm are actual <i>entities</i> which seem to embody, represent, or control these forces.<br /> <br /> The Trinity and the Triat are <i>linked</i>, but not <i>one-and-the-same</i>. Mages see one side of the coin; the Shifting Breeds see the other side of the coin. Heads is not Tails, and Tails is not Heads, but the Coin is the Coin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T13:14:33-07:00","id":167191,"title":"","content":"I remember the WW newsletter back when they mailed it, had an article on how to better fit one series with another and the idea was having Vampires come from the Wyrm. They're just reanimated corpses powered by this entity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T16:04:20-07:00","id":167319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oliver the Bold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/165057-the-triat-in-vtm?p=166993#post166993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wyrm is a laughable imitation of the Oblivion in Wraith, For even a defiled spirit fears the nothingness that awaits slumbering beyond (and within) all dogma.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, np. The Wyrm exists in a three-way suicide pact with itself - And since oblivion is a <i>product</i> of the Wyrm, even if it weren't locked into that suicide pact it would regard (inasmuch as such an entity can &quot;regard&quot; anything) its demise as inevitable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Changelings have a mirror of the Wyld in Glamour and the Weaver in Banality (a better mirror exists in the DA:Fae, but that would take awhile to explain) </div> </div> </div>Not so, with regard to Changeling. Banality and Glamour are wholly dependent on human interaction with something. Remember, the most glamor-filled moment in the 20th centiry happened because of television... but a room full of people watching Hoarders and cramming pizza in their face is undoubtedly banal. A Werewolg would find Disneyworld a horrifying, styfling weaver-pit with a gauntlet like a concrete wall... but a changeling would find it a wonderful place, brimming with glamour, so long as people are enjoying the park. Similarly, the Fomorians are undoubtedly something that the Garou would consider &quot;Of the Wyrm&quot; - but in changeling terms, they are exquisitely powerful fonts of glamour, godlike beings of pure dream.<br /> <br /> Banality and Glamour cross all boundaries - Book of the Wyld points out that the Irish potato famine was because of the Wyld touching a particular fungus... and I think we can all imagine that THAT was a hell of a banal time for Irish changelings...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampire has its own trinity of Caine, Lilith, and Lucifer if you want to look at it that way. Metaphysical natures notwithstanding, the universe is hardly an easy thing to deduce. </div> </div> </div>Of course when one considers that Vampires vastly predate these three beliefs...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T22:46:07-07:00","id":167589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/165057-the-triat-in-vtm?p=167319#post167319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really, np. The Wyrm exists in a three-way suicide pact with itself - And since oblivion is a <i>product</i> of the Wyrm, even if it weren't locked into that suicide pact it would regard (inasmuch as such an entity can &quot;regard&quot; anything) its demise as inevitable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like to direct attention to:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith: the Oblivion, Second Edition, page 284 &quot;Oblivion and the Wyrm&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Occult scholars in the know often confuse the Wyrm and Oblivion. Admittedly, each is a tremendous force, and in some ways a personification of destruction, but that is the only similarity. The Wyrm is active destruction and corruption, seeking to tear down all that exists. It is not content to wait for things to fall apart; it wishes to drag all down to ruin by the force of its actions.<br /> Oblivion, on the other hand, is patient, passive destruction. When things grow old and falter, as they all inevitably must, then and only then does Oblivion claim them. Even Spectres, in a very real sense, give themselves to Oblivion as opposed to being claimed by it.<br /> <b>At the end of all things, when the Wyrm has destroyed all else, it will seek to destroy the only thing that remains: itself. By doing so, it will gift itself to Oblivion.</b><br /> Some theorists postulate that the Wyrm and Oblivion are bound in a tight balance, a sort of yin-yang of destruction, and that as the Wyrm grew in power Oblivion was forced to grow to match it and maintain their eternal equilibrium. However, there is little (if any) evidence to support this hypothesis, and hard proof is likely to be hard to come by.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oblivion is the final boss of the cWoD, and it cannot be beat. It is the hungry mouth at the bottom of Creation, and it will not be sated until everything that ever was or will be is devoured, including the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> The Wyrm just brings it snacks.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T23:27:47-07:00","id":167645,"title":"","content":"CHEEE-TOHZ! *sounds of Oblivion/Grandma/vacuum cleaner*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T05:26:46-07:00","id":167778,"title":"","content":"I always imagined the metaphysics something like this:<br /> <br /> Imagine a simple geometric diamond pattern, one entity on top, three in the middle, and one on bottom. At the top would be &quot;the One&quot;, which is the source of all creation. At the bottom would be &quot;Oblivion&quot;, or the antithesis to the One and the absence of all creation. In the middle would be the Triat, which serves to process or filter the One through all the Tellurian and into Oblivion.<br /> <br /> When I imagine it this way, it isn't hard to see how multiple paradigms (Vampire (Corrupted Weaver), Mage (Dynamism), Werewolf (Wyld), Wraith (Oblivion), Changeling (Astral Umbra)) could all fit together in a loose way.<br /> <br /> It may not be perfect, but as others have said, with the in-universe imperfect understandings it makes enough sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}